{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528123-house-rule-touchstones","id":1528123,"title":"House Rule: Touchstones","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-06T13:14:12-08:00","id":1528123,"title":"House Rule: Touchstones","content":"My first house rule for Werewolf 5 will be this:<br /> <br /> &quot;Instead of being able to move a point of Hauglosk and Harano between each other by spending time with a Touchstone, you can remove a point of it instead.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T15:17:10-08:00","id":1528126,"title":"","content":"Honestly just removing the entire H/H mechanic entirely fixes a bunch of stuff and has literally zero impact on gameplay or immersion.<br /> <br /> It does take away from one of the very few things Touchstones do in W5 ( Increase your chances of gaining Harano and Hauglosk) but as you can likely guess removing them and replacing them with a group of NPCs that you character cares about without tacking a couple of mechanics onto them is the superior option for folks actually interested in roleplaying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T15:28:41-08:00","id":1528129,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the first house rule of W5's touchstone systems should be that the number of times you can use any Touchstone functions should increase scaled to how many of them you have... so there's actually a reason to have more than one at a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-07T02:05:29-08:00","id":1528144,"title":"","content":"Two things I'd add;<br /> <br /> -You can have more than one non-human Touchstone. Wolves do not die THAT much faster than humans.<br /> -A pack MUST have their totem as a Touchstone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-07T09:38:23-08:00","id":1528153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528123-house-rule-touchstones?p=1528129#post1528129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure the first house rule of W5's touchstone systems should be that the number of times you can use any Touchstone functions should increase scaled to how many of them you have... so there's actually a reason to have more than one at a time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, currently, mechanically, you are screwing yourself over massively if you take more than one Touchstone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-07T14:04:12-08:00","id":1528168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528123-house-rule-touchstones?p=1528126#post1528126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly just removing the entire H/H mechanic entirely fixes a bunch of stuff and has literally zero impact on gameplay or immersion.<br /> <br /> It does take away from one of the very few things Touchstones do in W5 ( Increase your chances of gaining Harano and Hauglosk) but as you can likely guess removing them and replacing them with a group of NPCs that you character cares about without tacking a couple of mechanics onto them is the superior option for folks actually interested in roleplaying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, no.<br /> <br /> It feels like it misses the entire point and just says, &quot;The roleplaying part isn't worth writing mechanics for unlike combat.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-07T14:47:15-08:00","id":1528170,"title":"","content":"In addition to the changes about how often you can use Touchstones-mechanics in relation to how many Touchstones has... I also would suggest that Touchstones shouldn't be about &quot;ties to humanity&quot; as the W5 corebook suggests. It made sense in VtM to do that - for obvious reasons since PCs literally have a trait on their char-sheet called Humanity. At its heart, Touchstones is about mandating players to pick NPCs that are close to the PC and fostering that relationship creates benefits. But why that relationship exists and in what form should vary from splat to splat. (In general, WOD5E could use a bit more openmindedness in regards to Touchstones.)<br /> <br /> My idea for what sort of Touchstones PCs should pick are non-Garou entities (either humans, wolves or spirits) who directly or indirectly participate in the same fight the Garou do. And the &quot;healing&quot;-mechanics of the Touchstones revolve around moods like camaraderie, solidarity and community. It's about participating in struggles and reminding yourself that you're not alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-07T23:47:32-08:00","id":1528203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528123-house-rule-touchstones?p=1528168#post1528168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, no.<br /> <br /> It feels like it misses the entire point and just says, &quot;The roleplaying part isn't worth writing mechanics for unlike combat.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Attaching a half-arsed on/off failure mechanic to something that should be a harrowing and deeply personal spiritual and psychological character Arc adds literally nothing to it and insults those who want to put the time and effort into properly portraying that sort of intrinsic struggle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-08T03:25:23-08:00","id":1528207,"title":"","content":"A slightly different way to put it? Mechanics are useful, and even good, but they still have to be the right mechanics for the job. Horror games tend to benefit a lot more from &quot;carrot&quot; mechanics than &quot;stick&quot; mechanics when they want to support deeper character explorations.<br /> <br /> It's really not complex: on average players will want to do things the game rewards them for doing, and will avoid doing things the game punishes them for doing. Executing it well is an entirely different matter of course, but the logic is pretty essential design.<br /> <br /> What I think trips up a lot of games is that the journey can be carrots and thus be perceived as rewarding, even if the end result is &quot;bad&quot; for the character.<br /> <br /> This is where just being able to remove Hauglosk/Harano points doesn't really address the underlying issue: gaining those boxes isn't fun, and having them isn't fun. There's no pay off for having your character dance the line between extremism and doomerism until one side finally captures them for good. The mechanics tell you to fight doing this as hard as possible, and that you need to avoid getting smacked with more of either if you want to have an enduring character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-08T06:23:40-08:00","id":1528208,"title":"","content":"Also, Hauglosk gains need an in-universe explanation that you can point to for NPCs to get some. Chronicle Tenets are neat but they don't exist in-universe. So like losing a Touchstone gives you Harano, losing something should give you Hauglosk.<br /> <br /> The problem arises from the fact that we already have in-book information that cannibalism, killing people for cash,etc. are okay and result in no Hauglosk.<br /> <br /> Maybe intentionally destroying something non-Wyrmy talisman/spirit in order to get to your goals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-08T07:44:32-08:00","id":1528211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528123-house-rule-touchstones?p=1528208#post1528208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem arises from the fact that we already have in-book information that cannibalism, killing people for cash,etc. are okay and result in no Hauglosk.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, Hauglosk isn't about morality, it's about excessive self-righteousness and blind suicidal pride.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-08T07:49:48-08:00","id":1528214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528123-house-rule-touchstones?p=1528211#post1528211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, Hauglosk isn't about morality, it's about excessive self-righteousness and blind suicidal pride.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm sure most Chronicle Tenets people will have will punish cannibalism, infecting innocent people and cold-blooded murder. Especially in WtA as opposed to VtM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-08T09:00:37-08:00","id":1528215,"title":"","content":"Chronicle Tenets is another area where I think W5 made the mistake of just copying V5. As it's presented in V5 the tenets are lists of actions characters &quot;should do&quot; or &quot;always do&quot;. And in V5 this fits into what those tenets are supposed to do. You're gonna think about specific actions that are important from a human perspective and so this naturally feeds into the idea of &quot;maintaining humanity&quot;. A WtA-game needs to reframe this in a way that makes sense for Garou and how in breaking those tenets Hauglosk is invited.<br /> <br /> My suggested solution is to make the tenets more specific as answers to pointed questions like &quot;What is the most important thing a Garou should do?&quot;, &quot;What is something a member of Tribe x should always do?&quot; or &quot;What should a member of Auspice y always do?&quot;... Something like this. And it doesn't matter whether it's group-based or individual-based... the point is to direct players' attention to a more Garou-specific perspective.<br /> <br /> Now I also would change the definition of Hauglosk if I were to run W5 again. I would make it about giving up on any greater good goals or duties/goals a Garou might have and just doing your own thing. It's a much broader definition because it's essentially about Garou (while not giving up on fighting and taking action (like with Harano) ) who are doing their own thing now and picking goals for themselves. That can be the berserk-crusade that's just looking to destroy stuff and the nihilistic endgoal of a good death with no pretense of trying to save the world. Or a pack holding territory and dominating it to feel secure (even though the territory doesn't even have a caern). Stuff like that. I think that also brings it more in line with Harano as two shades of the same idea of &quot;giving up&quot;. That way having Harano 4 and Hauglosk 4 feels less awkward as well.<br /> <br /> But let's take a look at the proposed examples for Chronicle Tenets in the W5 corebook:<br /> <br /> Environmentalist<ul><li>Never cause harm to Gaia</li> <li>Do not hoard resources</li> <li>Never put short-term gains ahead of long-term goals</li> </ul>Apocalypse Radicals<ul><li>Do not cling to the old ways</li> <li>Never kill an outsider</li> <li>Vengeance must be served\u200b</li> </ul>Traditionalist<ul><li>Uphold the Litany</li> <li>Heed your elders</li> <li>Only ritual challenge merits killing of other Garou\u200b</li> </ul>If you were to actually go for this idea of Hauglosk being &quot;fanatical self-righteousness&quot;, I think it would be a bit of a challenge why breaking some of these tenets would lead you down the path to Hauglosk.<br /> <br /> But the longer version explaining the process of picking Tenets really takes the cake by proposing a bad idea, I would say. These are the tenets:<ul><li>Punish the guilty</li> <li>Everyone deserves a second chance</li> <li>Never harm the innocent.\u200b</li> </ul>And here's what the text says: &quot;They are particularly interested in the seeming incongruity of punishing the guilty and offering the second chances \u2014 as Storyteller, Paula hopes this tension will set up some great conflicts within the pack.\u200b&quot; That sounds like a bad idea: So how are you gonna decide then what triggers the Hauglosk-tests? There's no need to outright create debate-topics like this in the game. Here, they should've just settled on &quot;Everyone deserves a second chance&quot; and then the ST can challenge that. And if it will create tension between the players, it will come from the players. There's no need for STs to engineer it like this.<br /> <br /> But I mentioned this last example from the book to underline why I'm in favor of getting more specific with Chronicle Tenets. Nobody needs an ST who believes they're playing 4D-chess by doing stuff like setting up contradictory Chronicle Tenets. It's dumb. Chronicle Tenets are supposed to be a mechanic, so clarity is more important. Any good group of players will generate more than enough story and conflict on their own without the ST sabotaging game-mechanics to artificially create conflicts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}